# What stays out of git. Everything a collaborator needs to build and launch is tracked:
# source, vendored dependencies (Deps/release, git submodules), the FX donor trees and their
# compiled pack (FX/compiled, git LFS) and the ragdoll animation data (git LFS). See
# Docs/setup/collaborator-setup.md. Generated output belongs under build/ or Automation/runs/.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build outputs
/build
/build-*/
/cmake-build-*/
/ipch
/out
/packages
AfxCppCli/build/
ShaderBuilder/obj/
FilmmakerDemoInfoGo/build/
FilmmakerDemoInfoGo/out.json
FilmmakerDemoInfoGo/err.txt
FX/tools/ragdoll-loosen/bin/
FX/tools/ragdoll-loosen/obj/
build-*.bat.log
*.pdb
# Archived release symbols (Automation/tools/archive-symbols.ps1): keep them, never commit them.
/Automation/symbols/
*.ilk
*.obj
*.pch
*.idb
*.tlog

# Go tool binaries, wherever `go build` was run from (helpers and their per-subtool scanners).
FilmmakerDemoInfoGo/**/*.exe
FilmmakerDemoRepairGo/**/*.exe
FilmmakerDemoKeyframesGo/**/*.exe

# Rust
Lib/**/target/

# Node / package managers
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Python caches
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache/

